.TH PRINTF "1" "September 2026" "GNU coreutils 9.12" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
printf \- format and print data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B printf
\fI\,FORMAT \/\fR[\fI\,ARGUMENT\/\fR]...
.br
.B printf
\fI\,OPTION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Print ARGUMENT(s) according to FORMAT, or execute according to OPTION:
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/printf#printf--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/printf#printf--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
.PP
FORMAT controls the output as in C printf.  Interpreted sequences are:
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 8
\e"
double quote
.TP 8
\e\e
backslash
.TP 8
\ea
alert (bell)
.TP 8
\eb
backspace
.TP 8
\ec
produce no further output
.TP 8
\ee
escape
.TP 8
\ef
form feed
.TP 8
\en
new line
.TP 8
\er
carriage return
.TP 8
\et
horizontal tab
.TP 8
\ev
vertical tab
.TP 8
\eNNN
byte with octal value NNN (1 to 3 digits)
.TP 8
\exHH
byte with hexadecimal value HH (1 to 2 digits)
.TP 8
\euHHHH
Unicode (ISO/IEC 10646) character with hex value HHHH (4 digits)
.TP 12
\eUHHHHHHHH
Unicode character with hex value HHHHHHHH (8 digits)
.PD
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 8
%%
a single %
.TP 8
%b
ARGUMENT as a string with '\e' escapes interpreted,
except that octal escapes should have a leading 0 like \e0NNN
.TP 8
%q
ARGUMENT is printed in a format that can be reused as shell input,
escaping non\-printable characters with the POSIX $'' syntax
.PD
.PP
and all C \fBprintf\fP(3) format specifications ending with one of diouxXfaAeEgGcs,
with ARGUMENTs converted to proper type first.
FORMAT is reused to convert all specified arguments.
The following table shows supported conversion specifiers,
with examples including usage of width, precision, and flags.
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 12
CONVERSION
Shell format example        Output
.TP 12
%s
\&'[%10s]' 'left pad'         [  left pad]
.TP 12
%s
\&'[%\-10s]' 'right pad'       [right pad ]
.TP 12
%c %s
\&'%c %.3s' un unibyte        u uni
.PD
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 12
%d %i
"%'d ;%04i" 1234 '\-1'       1,234 ;\-001
.TP 12
%o
\&'%#o' $((2#110100100))      0644
.TP 12
%u
\&'%u' 0xFFFFFFFF             4294967295
.TP 12
%x
\&'0x%08x' 11259375           0x00abcdef
.PD
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 12
%a %f
\&'%1$a %1$f' 0.0009765625    0x8p\-13 0.000977
.TP 12
%e %f
\&'%1$e %1$f' 123.456789      1.234568e+02 123.456789
.TP 12
%g
\&'%1$g %1$.2g' 1.2345678e3   1234.57 1.2e+03
.PD
.PP
.PD 0
.TP 12
%b
\&'%bfoo' 'bar\ecbaz' qux      bar
.TP 12
%q
\&'%q ' 'a' \e;b $'c\en'        a ';b' 'c'$'\en'
.PD
.PP
